  "note": "Annual election of one third (five seats). J. W. Pollock, town clerk, received nominations on Thursday 5 January 1933: four outgoing members (Greer, Hill, Lunn, Bryans) and Fred A. Monroe, a new member; J. S. Carrick, the fifth outgoing member, did not seek re-election. \"There were no other papers received, and consequently there will be no contest.\" (15 January 1933 was a Sunday; the date used is the following Monday.) Labels: the Lurgan council was wholly Unionist in this period."
